<!-- 08 HOW IT WORKS -->
<section class="wrap band stack" style="gap:clamp(28px,4vw,44px)">
  <div class="stack" style="gap:14px">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2 class="h2" style="max-width:22ch">One conversation. One written plan within 24 hours.</h2>
  </div>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><span class="n">01</span><h3 class="h3">Tell us what you&rsquo;re planning</h3><p class="p p--s">Share the date, approximate guest count, venue and anything you already know about the celebration.</p></li>
    <li><span class="n">02</span><h3 class="h3">Speak to the person who will plan your food</h3><p class="p p--s">We talk about your family, what you like to eat, the venue and how you want the celebration to feel.</p></li>
    <li><span class="n">03</span><h3 class="h3">Receive your written plan</h3><p class="p p--s">Within 24 hours, we send the written plan for the celebration - the menu journey, live experiences, service style and presentation.</p></li>
    <li><span class="n">04</span><h3 class="h3">Taste. Refine. Confirm.</h3><p class="p p--s">You taste the dishes, we make the final refinements and then lock the experience for the day.</p></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<!-- 09 ONE PLAN -->
<section class="band band--card">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="stack" style="gap:14px">
      <h2 class="h2" style="max-width:16ch">One plan. Everything working together.</h2>
      <p class="p" style="max-width:40ch">Not separate dishes selected from a list. One experience, planned around a single idea.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="incl incl--1col">
      <li><strong>The culinary idea</strong> <span>&mdash; The family, the child and the celebration translated into one coherent idea for the food.</span></li>
      <li><strong>The menu journey</strong> <span>&mdash; What begins the evening, what is passed, what guests discover live, when mains open and how dessert closes the celebration.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Passed canap&eacute;s</strong> <span>&mdash; Bites designed to reach guests wherever they are in the room rather than making them search for food.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Live experiences</strong> <span>&mdash; Chef-led counters designed around theatre, freshness and interaction.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Grazing</strong> <span>&mdash; A generous table guests can discover casually while mingling over drinks.</span></li>
      <li><strong>The plated buffet</strong> <span>&mdash; The abundance and choice of a buffet, with mains plated and served by our attendants instead of guests queuing with plates.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Presentation &amp; styling</strong> <span>&mdash; How the food, displays, counters, tableware and presentation language come together visually.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Service choreography</strong> <span>&mdash; How food moves through the room, where attendants are positioned and how each stage of the evening transitions into the next.</span></li>
      <li><strong>The dessert finale</strong> <span>&mdash; A closing food moment designed as part of the evening, not simply another counter at the back of the room.</span></li>
      <li><strong>The team on the day</strong> <span>&mdash; Chefs, service staff, counter attendants and one Virtuoso lead responsible for the food and service from start to finish.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Bar</strong> <span>&mdash; Cocktail and beverage experiences can be added where required.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 10 FAQ -->
<section class="wrap band split">
  <h2 class="h2" style="max-width:14ch">Questions families ask.</h2>
  <dl class="faq">
    <div><dt>What does the first call involve?</dt><dd>Around twenty minutes with the person who will plan your food. We ask about your family, the venue, what you enjoy eating and how you want the celebration to feel. You also get to understand how we work before deciding whether you would like to go ahead.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>What is in the 24-hour plan?</dt><dd>A written plan for the celebration covering the culinary idea, menu journey, live experiences, plated buffet, service style and presentation - along with an indicative cost for the guest count discussed. The 24 hours start once we have agreed the size and scale of the celebration on the call, not when you send the form.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>What do you mean by a plated buffet?</dt><dd>You still have the generosity and variety of a beautifully presented main-course spread. The difference is in the service: our attendants plate the food for your guests instead of guests moving through a self-service buffet line.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Do you only do plated buffets?</dt><dd>No. The service style is designed around the celebration. Depending on the venue and brief, the evening may combine passed canap&eacute;s, grazing, live counters, plated buffet service and other formats.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Do you do celebrations under 50 guests?</dt><dd>Our first-birthday offering is primarily designed for celebrations of 50 guests or more. For smaller private celebrations, speak to us and we will tell you whether the format is suitable.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Will we be chased after we enquire?</dt><dd>No. One person from Virtuoso calls you once. If you would like to continue, you tell us. If not, that is the end of it.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>

